    <string name="ui_room_heading">Calibrate for my speakers and room</string>
    <string name="ui_room_hint">Plays pink noise for about 10 seconds and records it with the microphone to find peaks in your speaker and room response. It then proposes a gentle correction: mostly cuts (up to 9 dB) and only small boosts (up to 3 dB). The microphone permission is asked only now, and the audio is analysed in memory, never saved or sent. Use a quiet room, put the phone where you listen, and use speakers rather than headphones. Phone microphones are not perfectly flat, so judge the result by ear.</string>
